No. The semicolons and capitalized 'OR' operators denote mutually exclusive qualifying criteria. 

A claim qualifies for Path 2 if it meets any of the following independent conditions:
1. Gross loss between $50,000 and $250,000;
2. A temperature-logger discrepancy;
3. Multi-jurisdictional salvage.

Because the temperature discrepancy criterion stands alone, it triggers Path 2 automatically, even though the gross loss ($38,000) falls below the standard $50,000 financial threshold.

